since her film debut in 1994 scarlett  johansson has become one of the most  recognizable and successful actors in  hollywood  here are a few of the most critically  acclaimed roles that johansen has  portrayed throughout her career  from independent efforts to blockbuster  smash hits  still johansen's best reviewed film on  rotten tomatoes  lost in translation was hailed as a  revelation upon its release in 2003  both for its leading performance by bill  murray and for sophia coppola's stylish  and elegant direction  however it's johansen's performance that  gives the movie the profound sense of  existential loneliness  that coppola's films are known for  johansen plays charlotte a recent  college graduate visiting japan  adrift in her life and uncertain about  her future charlotte befriends  fading actor bob played by murray who  feels similarly lost as he flounders  through middle age  the two keep each other company for a  few days in tokyo forming a deep bond  over their mutual sense of alienation  the film landed oscar nominations for  best picture best director and  screenplay for coppola and best actor  for murray  although johansen was unfortunately  snubbed regardless lost in translation  was declared an instant classic by many  critics  terry lawson of the detroit press summed  up the general appeal  writing there is real magic afoot in  lost in translation  the sort that is created not at the wave  of a wizard's wand but by the coming  together of two wayward souls  although johansen didn't get much screen  time in avengers infinity war her iconic  portrayal of the mcu's natasha romanov  otherwise known as black widow played a  pivotal role in the grand cinematic  finale that was  avengers and game as one of the few  avengers left standing after the snap  johansson plays a hero worn down by loss  and despair  endgame provides black widow with an  emotional send-off as she  spoiler alert sacrifices herself to help  save the world  however the cosmic dust had barely  settled on end game  before marvel head honcho kevin feige  announced a black widow standalone movie  in july 2019.  it may have taken nine years since the  first avengers movie for johansen to get  her own film  but it's certainly better late than  never for her legions of fans  although the movie was delayed multiple  times black widow is currently slated to  hit theaters in july 2021  while johansen is primarily known for  her live action work  she has also lent her voice to a number  of prominent films  including the jungle book isle of dogs  and the spongebob squarepants movie  however her most acclaimed voiceover  work to date was her role as an  artificially intelligent operating  system  in her written and directed by spike  jones the near-future sci-fi film which  won an oscar for jones original  screenplay  chronicles the romantic misadventures of  sad sack writer theodore twombly played  by joaquin phoenix  who finds himself falling in love with  the artificially intelligent virtual  assistant  samantha it's easy to see why theodore  falls for samantha  even though she has no physical form  samantha's soulful personality  humor empathy curiosity and intelligence  can  all be felt through johansen's voice  alone samantha also conveys a certain  wistfulness about the experience of  living that feels all too human  despite her artificial nature critics  were charmed and dazzled by jones vision  with empire magazine declaring jones has  made a sweet  smart silly serious film for our times  only set in the future alongside taiko  ytt's jojo rabbid  johansen earned one of her first two  oscar nominations in 2019  for noah bombach's marriage story a  searing portrayal of divorce  marriage story sees johansen play nicole  a former teen star married to charlie a  theater director  played by fellow oscar nominee adam  driver when nicole wants to move to los  angeles to advance her career  even though charlie wants to stay in new  york their already troubled union begins  to slide towards dissolution  bombach himself has said that the film  is semi-autobiographical  partially based on his divorce from  actor jennifer jason lee  while bombach's sympathies are clearly  biased in charlie's favor  johansson still brings an enormous  amount of sympathy and relatability to  the character of nicole  critics gushed about the film and the  performances with moira macdonald of the  seattle times raving  johansson and driver are remarkably  heartbreakingly good in every scene  ghost world was an early critical  success for johansen  and an important transition from her  career as a child actor though she was  only 16 upon its release  the 2001 movie co-written and directed  by terry swygoff  is a mature and serious film about two  young women facing an  uncertain world after their high school  graduation for johansen  ghostworld adapted from daniel klo's  comic book series 8-ball  was also her first foray into a genre  that would catapult her into the highest  ranks of international stardom  the movie stars thora birch as enid a  classic generation x archetype  ironic lost and darkly cynical johansson  plays the role of her best friend  rebecca who is slightly more tethered to  reality and their difference in outlook  eventually leads the girls to having a  falling out  some people are okay but mostly i just  feel like poisoning everybody  ghost world was not very popular with  audiences but it was widely praised by  critics who appreciated its offbeat  sense of humor  emotional honesty and unsparing  depiction of teenage angst  as roger ebert wrote i wanted to hug  this movie it takes such a risky journey  and never steps wrong  it creates specific original believable  lovable characters  and meanders with them through their  inconsolable days never losing its sense  of humor  the culmination of phase one of the mcu  the avengers  proved that marvel movies were here to  stay the movie grossed more than 1.5  billion dollars and was beloved by both  audiences and critics  with a certified fresh score of 91 on  the tomato meter with almost 25 minutes  of screen time  johansen's black widow is the third most  prominent character in the avengers  after iron man and captain america even  if her role in the avengers isn't as  dramatically juicy as the one she gets  in captain america the winter soldier  she still gets her fair share of heroic  moments especially as the avengers save  new york from thor's brother loki  and his legions of alien henchmen in the  final act  while critics lauded the movie's action  and special effects  many were equally impressed by the  performances of the avengers themselves  in his review of the film for the  atlantic  christopher orr wrote that johansen's  black widow is quote  far more interesting than she was in  iron man 2 and that the cast in general  is excellent down the line and plays  well together even  perhaps especially when their characters  don't  the 2014 captain america sequel the  winter soldier was something of a  welcome departure for the marvel  cinematic universe  phase two of the mcu had gotten off to a  bit of a rocky start with a successful  but uninspired iron man 3 and the  middling  thor the dark world both films had done  well at the box office  but it was clear the mcu needed a fresh  approach the winter soldier delivered by  fusing its typical superhero fare  with elements of the spy thriller genre  popularized by classic films like  the parallax view and three days of the  condor critics were impressed with the  winter soldier's action set pieces  and its topical narrative about the  price of freedom and security in the age  of surveillance  as black widow is the primary avenger  featured alongside captain america in  the film  johansson benefited from the film's  acclaim and was subsequently prominently  featured in avengers age of ultron  but while that film's reputation may  have faded over the years the winter  soldier has emerged as an  mcu favorite with johansson providing a  big part of its continuing appeal  among both casual viewers and marvel  fanatics  johansson reunited with iron man 2  director john favreau  for his 2014 passion project about a  middle-aged chef  and his bold attempt to reignite his  creative spirit favreau plays the  titular chef carl casper  and johansson is molly the hostess at  the restaurant casper worked at for 10  years before his very public midlife  crisis meltdown  you're not getting to me okay okay  you're not getting to me  favreau and johansen have a natural  chemistry in this film  stuffed with stars as it is with  delectable dishes including dustin  hoffman  sophia vergara and robert downey jr  johansen's molly is just as appealing as  any of the cuisine on display which is  no small feat in a movie guaranteed to  have you craving a gourmet meal from  beginning to end  critics were mostly charmed by the light  comedy which sits at 87 percent on the  tomato meter  praising the cast the soundtrack and of  course the delicious looking food  writing in little white lies chris blum  called the movie a  sassy and mouth-watering concoction  bursting with flavor  given her comic abilities and previous  experience as a sultry femme fatale type  in post-war los angeles in the black  dahlia  johansson was a no-brainer to join  george clooney channing tatum  rafe fines francis mcdormand and tilda  swinton  in the all-star cast of hail caesar a  coen brothers comedy set in 1950's  hollywood  johansen plays deanna morin a character  based off of actress esther williams  who performs in synchronized swimming  routines that were popular at the time  when diana's unplanned pregnancy  threatens her career and the studio's  bottom line  a studio fixer played by josh brolin is  tasked with covering it up  although audiences had mixed reactions  critics enjoyed the movie  praising the coen brothers playful  spirit its performances  and its nostalgic reflection on  hollywood's golden age  the guardian's mark commode wrote of the  film as a whole its utterly chaotic and  ridiculously indulgent and it would  amount to intolerable cruelty  where hale sees her not so consistently  uproariously  affectionately funny johansen has carved  out a niche for herself in the science  fiction genre more than most of her  fellow a-list actors  in addition to her many appearances in  the mcu and her  the actor has also headlined michael  bay's the island  the surprise global hit lucy and the  controversial live-action remake of  ghost in the shell  but while under the skin is sci-fi this  indie film has little else in common  with those big budget commercial affairs  a product of gorilla filmmaking under  the skin surrounded johansen with real  people  not actors and captured much of its  unscripted footage with hidden cameras  the movie is light on action in favor of  a detached cerebral story about a  feminine alien  played by johansen who uses her good  looks to hunt down men throughout  scotland  and lure them back to her dark lair to  consume them however as soon as she  appears to identify more traditionally  as a human woman  she finds herself going from predator to  prey although a box office failure  under the skin found favor with critics  and scholars who read it as a feminist  allegory about gender inequality  it also showed off johansen's continued  desire to take on challenging  and cryptic roles outside of the usual  blockbusters  taika waititi won the best adapted  screenplay oscar for his anti-hate  satire  jojo rabbit which made waves upon its  release for its unique take on world war  ii the film stars roman griffin davis as  the titular jojo a young german boy  whose imaginary best friend is a  caricature of adolf hitler  played by ytt himself while the film was  marketed as a comedy  johansson's role as jojo's mother rosie  serves as the emotional core of the film  as she struggles to balance being a  single mother to a blindly nationalist  child  with hiding a jewish teenager from the  nazi forces  critics and audiences alike enjoyed jojo  rabbit praising its humor  charm and anti-hate message however as  with many comic takes on hitler and  nazis  jojo rabbit generated his fair share of  controversy  with joanne laurier writing that the  movie inadvertently or not  trivializes nazism and turns people away  from a study of the concrete historical  processes that produced such horrific  carnage  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stuff are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  you
 

